1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
This is not a static mock or slide deck. The product is running on
Google Cloud Run, and the operational badge comes from the live API.

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:29,000
ProfileProof canonicalizes the LinkedIn URL, verifies identity,
normalizes professional fields, and attaches clear provenance.

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The safe sample exercises the deployed API and complete interface
without exposing anyone's private data.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Raw JSON exposes source mode, warnings, limitations,
request ID, cache state, and the versioned schema.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:18,000
This verified real-profile response returned HTTP 200, public professional
fields, explicit provenance, and cached true on the repeat request.

6
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Invalid input fails before reaching LinkedIn. Redaction, session expiry,
schema changes, and upstream throttling remain explicit.

7
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The failed attempt was a LinkedIn throttle. The patch preserves it as 429,
adds Retry-After, and opens a cooldown circuit instead of retrying blindly.

8
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:05,000
LinkedIn blocks Google data-center egress, so Cloud Run uses an
automatically discovered residential worker on this Mac.

9
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:16,000
If the Mac is off, GCP stays healthy but real acquisition reports
provider unavailable. An always-on home worker removes this limitation.

10
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,700
Typed data, verified identity, transparent provenance,
observability, caching, and honest failure behavior.
